<%- include('header') %><main class="reading"><div class="eyebrow">PLAIN ENGLISH PRIVACY</div><h1>Your memory.<br>Your control.</h1><p class="lede">Brain keeps the information you and your assistants choose to put here. You can take it with you or delete it.</p><section><h2>What we store</h2><p>Your account email, an Argon2id password hash, sign-in sessions, assistant connection labels, OAuth client records, and hashed access credentials. We also store notes, handoffs, shared facts, memory snapshots, conversation sessions, background tasks and their results, token usage, overnight reflections and checks, workspace files, and an activity history.</p><p>Connected assistants can read the shared facts and snapshots in your brain. Notes are visible to their recipients and sender; broadcast notes are visible to all your assistants. Only connect clients and assistants you trust.</p></section><section><h2>Where it lives</h2><p>One server in Helsinki, Finland, operated by <a href="https://arxsable.ai">Arx Sable LLC</a>, Banning, California. Hosting is provided by Hetzner. No content is sent to advertising or analytics services.</p><p>When you use reasoning, background work, automatic summaries, or overnight updates, Brain sends the relevant question and saved context to Anthropic. An optional OpenAI connection can provide the overnight second look. These providers process that context to return the result. Research can make web searches and fetch public webpages. Email delivery uses the configured mail service when you request it.</p><p>The assistants and MCP clients you connect receive the information they request. Their own providers’ privacy policies apply to copies they receive. Brain cannot delete information already returned to them.</p></section><section><h2>What we do not do</h2><p>No analytics. No ad tracking. No sale of your data. No sharing with advertisers or data brokers. Reasoning, hosting, research, and requested email delivery use the services described above. We use essential sign-in and security cookies. Request logs contain operational details, never note content, passwords, or raw tokens.</p></section><section><h2>Export, revoke, delete</h2><p>Saved memories and snapshots remain until you clear them or delete your account; they do not expire automatically.</p><p><a href="/account">Your account</a> lets you download everything in one JSON file, rename or revoke assistant connections, clear one brain’s content while preserving your account, or delete your account. Saved files are available as separate downloads in the dashboard. Deletion removes your live records immediately. Same-server recovery backups expire within 14 days; deleted data could remain in those backups until they expire. We do not restore a deleted account for normal operation. A service-wide daily usage total may remain after content is cleared or an account is deleted. It contains no account identifier or memory content and protects the shared spending limit.</p></section><section><h2>Know the limits</h2><p>Brain is open-source, vibecoded software. The specification was drafted with Claude and the implementation written with OpenAI Codex. Public deployment and automated tests do not establish a completed independent human security review. Review the <a href="https://github.com/Oscar-G13/sesame-brain">code</a> before sharing sensitive information. This service is for adults 18 and older.</p><p>No email verification or password recovery is available in v1. Keep your password safe.</p></section><p class="small muted">Effective November 2, 2026. Questions or security reports: <a href="mailto:security@arxsable.ai">security@arxsable.ai</a>. Unofficial; not affiliated with or endorsed by Sesame AI Inc.</p></main><%- include('footer') %>
